WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.395
[MUSIC]

00:00:06.395 --> 00:00:11.397
Folks would take a growth mindset,
see the challenges they're

00:00:11.397 --> 00:00:16.399
facing as something that they
could develop enough to achieve or

00:00:16.399 --> 00:00:19.269
overcome or master or learn from, so

00:00:19.269 --> 00:00:25.820
that a failure from a broke mindset
perspective is an opportunity to learn.

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:30.810
One of the thing that goes on when you're
learning from the context of another

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:32.880
people who are different from you,

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:37.199
you are confronted with experiences
that you would never have had.

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:41.200
Now, if you're in a group with
a lot of people who look and

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:46.620
have very different experiences and now
you begin to share those experiences, you

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:52.590
gain from that living knowledge about what
it is like to be a very different person.

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:56.300
And they're saying, well, here's what
happened when we used that approach.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:58.170
And somebody else who raised
their hands and say, yeah, but

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:00.670
here's what happened when
we used that approach.

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:02.330
And they're so different.

00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:06.850
And that's incredibly educational
from a developmental perspective and

00:01:06.850 --> 00:01:11.270
make sure begin to realize things that
you have been taking for granted or

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:13.490
possibilities that you've never consider.

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:18.220
I remember hearing a Ukrainian
mass retailer comparing

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:23.500
what was going on in his organization
to an executive from Lululemon.

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:26.710
And the learning that came out
of that interaction was amazing.

00:01:26.710 --> 00:01:30.200
That diversity allows you to
start thinking of possibilities.

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:34.030
And remember, it's thinking of
possibilities that makes it possible for

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:36.629
us to engage in the developmental
approach to work.

00:01:38.010 --> 00:01:41.390
&gt;&gt; Transform your approach to
leadership excellence and development.

00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:44.676
Learn more about SEP,
the Stanford Executive Program.

